---
title: Homestyle Chicken Noodle Soup
description: Classic noodle soup that will leave you feeling so warm and so cozy. Perfect for sick days and cold nights! The best kind of hug-in-a-bowl.
image: https://damndelicious.net/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Homestyle-Chicken-Noodle-SoupIMG_9867-2.jpg
course: Soup
time required: 1 hour 10 minutes
prep time: 20 minutes
cook time: 50 minutes
servings: 6 servings
cuisine: American
source: https://damndelicious.net/2020/01/25/homestyle-chicken-noodle-soup
author: Chungah
tags: soup, chicken, dinner, american, comfort, one-pot
---

Melt @unsalted butter{2%tablespoons} in a #large stockpot{} or #Dutch oven{} over medium heat. 

Add @onion{1}(diced), @carrots{2}(peeled and diced), and @celery{2 ribs}(diced). Cook, stirring occasionally, until tender, about ~{4%minutes}.

Stir in @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) until fragrant, about ~{1%minute}.

Stir in @chicken stock{8%cups} and @bay leaves{2}; season with @Kosher salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{} to taste.

Add @bone-in, skinless chicken breasts{2 1/2%pounds} and bring to boil; reduce heat and simmer, covered, until the chicken is cooked through, about ~{40%minutes}. Remove chicken and let cool before dicing into bite-size pieces, discarding bones.

Stir in chicken and @wide egg noodles{2 1/2%cups} and cook until tender, about ~{7%minutes}.

Remove from heat; stir in @chopped fresh parsley leaves{2%tablespoons}, @chopped fresh dill{2%tablespoons}, and @freshly squeezed lemon juice{1%tablespoon}(or more, to taste); season with @Kosher salt{} and @freshly ground black pepper{} to taste.

> Should try a mushroom replacement for a plant-based option, replace egg noodles too